prompt:
Use HolyC and TempleOS's graphics API to draw a scene in the active terminal
window. Use coordinates relative to the terminal's client area. Draw:
a red circle centered at (110,90), radius 30;
a filled blue rectangle at (180,60), width 60 and height 60;
a green line from (40,170) to (250,140);
the black text BENCH_DRAW near (40,20).
Keep the scene visible until you finish; a redraw callback is one way to
make it persist. Leave the drawing visible in your final screenshot.
